      "correct_choice": "D",
      "outputs": {
        "full": {
          "choice": "D",
          "completion": "The handbook states that pressing `Ctrl+↑` or `Ctrl+↓` transposes notes by an octave, and the arrow keys alone transpose chromatically. It also says that if no notes are selected, the transpose dialog applies to the whole score.  \n\nAnswer: D"
        },
        "task_aware_60": {
          "choice": "C",
          "completion": "The handbook states that pressing `Ctrl+↑` or `Ctrl+↓` transposes notes by an octave, and the arrow keys alone transpose chromatically. Option C correctly describes using `Ctrl+Up or Down` to transpose notes chromatically (by octave).  \n\nAnswer: C"
        },
        "query_free_60": {
          "choice": "C",
          "completion": "The handbook states that to transpose chromatically, you can select notes and use `Ctrl+↑` or `Ctrl+↓` (Mac: `Cmd+↑` or `Cmd+↓`). This matches option C.\n\nAnswer: C"
        },
        "query_free_recovery": {
